152	/// Start the program a definition names, with the environment it declares.
153	///
154	/// A tool server gets the credentials its own configuration names, and no others.
155	///
156	/// Not `env_clear()`. A tool server needs PATH to find its interpreter, HOME for
157	/// its package caches, LANG for its encoding, and an allowlist of that would be
158	/// long, runtime-specific, and wrong the first time someone adds a Python server --
159	/// exactly the enumeration this codebase has been burned by before. Removing the
160	/// credentials leaves everything a runtime needs untouched.
161	///
162	/// The removal comes first and `envs` second, so a server that declares one of
163	/// these gets it back. That is the whole routing mechanism: `github` says
164	/// `GH_TOKEN: ${GH_TOKEN}` and receives it, `shell` says nothing and does not.
165	///
166	/// All three pipes, whichever transport follows. What stdout then means differs --
167	/// see `connect`.
168	fn spawn_process(config: &ToolDef) -> Result<Child> {
